  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: Empower Inclusion: Combating Gender and Disability Disinformation in Georgia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Anti-Gender Disinformation (GID) Project in Georgia addresses the harmful impact of disinformation on gender equality and marginalized groups, including women, youth, and individuals with disabilities. Through targeted activities, the project seeks to raise awareness, promote positive narratives, and empower communities to combat disinformation effectively. 
This project plans to use two days workshops with the goal to find more supporters and empower the stakeholders. The target groups for the workshops are: disability community, CSOs and civic activists. The goal of those workshops are not just raise awareness about GID, but empower the community.</narrative>
  </description>
